3. The block on the wall. If one block of each group has (1 + e) times the mean error of a block and the rest have the mean,
   measured error over formula is 1 + e over the number of blocks in a group. The table gives e.
   For the scalar rule: if one weight of each group has no error, measured over formula is 1 - f over the group size. The table gives f.
   family | group | blocks in a group | e for Z8 | e for E8 | f for X
      G |   8 | 1 | +0.249 | +0.249 | +0.65
      G |  32 | 4 | +0.250 | +0.249 | +0.26
      G | 128 | 16 | +0.254 | +0.242 | -0.20
      G |   R | 256 | +0.320 | +0.166 | -0.80
      T |   8 | 1 | +0.258 | +0.250 | +0.91
      T |  32 | 4 | +0.312 | +0.249 | +1.20
      T | 128 | 16 | +0.733 | +0.252 | +4.19
      T |   R | 256 | +28.254 | +0.215 | +205.38
   real |   8 | 1 | +0.297 | +0.250 | +0.97
   real |  32 | 4 | +0.489 | +0.252 | +1.66
   real | 128 | 16 | +1.562 | +0.262 | +7.25
   real |   R | 64/256 | +8.427 | +0.335 | +47.59
   A point on the surface of a cell in n dimensions is, in the mean, (n + 2) / n times as far in squared distance as a point inside it: e = 2/8 = 0.25.

