6. The scale term for regions of other shapes with the volume of the E8 code's region, in dB. Not a run of any codebook:
   each line is 10 log10 of (sum of squared scalar steps over sum of squared scales), with the scale the smallest at which the region holds every block of the group.
   ball: the scale is set by the longest block. cross-polytope: by the block with the largest sum of sizes of its entries. The cube is the scalar rule, 0 by definition.
   family | group | E8 region (measured in the run) | ball | cross-polytope | matrices
